  "finding_disposition": [
    {
      "boundary": "This is static preservation of an already-caught primary against the newly added bookkeeping path. It is not a universal allocation-equivalence proof, actual injected-failure run, or complete original cleanup qualification.",
      "evidence": [
        "Three source-owned raw error slots and a conservative secondary_clear flag exist before any secondary handler.",
        "Each complete newly added secondary-handler body is now inside try/except BaseException: pass. This includes flag write, raw-slot write, exception traceback access, tuple construction, record lookup and list append.",
        "The handler writes secondary_clear=False, then its designated raw exception slot, before attempting the optional allocating journal. The flag is never reset by the new source.",
        "The outer entry still has a bare raise after its guarded adapter-exit handler. An error from the newly added bookkeeping is swallowed by that handler and therefore cannot replace the already-caught original P via the previously identified path. Nested except completion restores the enclosing handled exception for that bare raise.",
        "Observation export requires flag True, all three raw slots None, and an empty journal. A failed optional journal does not turn a recorded secondary into an exportable clean state."
      ],
      "id": "G12-CANDIDATE-001",
      "predecessor_status": "REJECTED_CONDITIONAL_PRIMARY_MASKING_PATH",
