      "boundary": "Source-level capture/currentness ownership is established for this exact successor delta. No target graph was constructed or run, and stage/source adoption remains separate.",
      "evidence": [
        "Already-captured _g12_helper_current now directly loads _g12_continuation_entry, _g12_after_original_exit and _g12_original_terminal_custody. The AST verifies each name is unshadowed by a parameter/local/exception binding, and each is required to be exact FunctionType with the actual driver globals.",
        "The original main_epoch -> _g12_bind_locals -> _g12_helper_current and Phases.call -> _g12_after_phase -> _g12_helper_current source edges remain unchanged. The new references therefore extend the existing initial driver graph to all three actual outer functions.",
        "The unchanged cache selector captures the actual selected handler from the genuine driver namespace. selected_commit closes over that handler before product publication; the captured handler reaches _g12_helper_current, so the same three references also extend the original C3 product closure graph.",
        "The unchanged authority raw_function_record collects direct code names and capture_graph follows function-valued effective globals/closures. Its existing current checks retain function fields, code, globals, defaults, closure/attribute identities and effective-global bindings. No generalized loader, late recapture or fabricated source record was introduced.",
        "The actual top-level guard invokes the same _g12_continuation_entry global; entry invokes the same _g12_after_original_exit global; exit invokes the same _g12_original_terminal_custody global. Both variants have these identical source relationships."
      ],
